{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01TCtQkSZuxM2YYi5bKabc3i","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: go-unix-utils is an experiment in specification-driven development. It derives formal specifications from C source code of GNU utilities, generates Go implementations using an AI orchestrator (mage-claude-orchestrator), and verifies correctness through differential testing against Homebrew GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). Key components: `cmd/` (per-utility Go implementations), `pkg/testutils/` (differential testing harness), `pkg/sys/` (syscall abstractions), `pkg/format/` (output formatting), `magefiles/` (build targets), and `docs/` (specs, PRDs, use cases, test suites).\n\n**Current state**: In the current generation, foundational infrastructure is complete — `pkg/testutils`, `pkg/sys`, `pkg/format` all have implementations and tests. `cmd/ts` is implemented. The remaining work in `rel00.0` is magefiles (build infrastructure, non-blocking for utility work). The next release `rel01.1` has three utilities pending: wc, cat, sponge.\n\n**Current release**: `rel01.1` — wc (uc001), cat (uc002), and sponge (uc003) all have specs written but no code generated yet.\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\n`rel00.0-uc001-magefiles` is technically the earliest incomplete use case, but magefiles are build infrastructure that don't block utility implementation (the stitch agent uses `go build` directly). The highest-value next task is starting `rel01.1` with `wc` — the first utility in that batch. All dependencies are satisfied: `pkg/testutils`, `pkg/sys`, and `pkg/format` are implemented, and `cmd/ts` provides a pattern reference.\n\nFollowing P2 (split implementation and tests) and P8 (implementation before tests), I propose the wc implementation task. Tests will be a separate follow-up task.\n\n## Proposed Tasks\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"rel01.1-uc001 wc: Implement cmd/wc word count utility\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (cmd/ component structure and conventions)\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/ (find the wc PRD -- glob for prd*wc*.yaml -- read all requirements and flag specifications)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel01.1-uc001-wc.yaml (wc use case and execution path)\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel-01.1.yaml (test inputs and expected behaviors for wc)\n      - cmd/ts/main.go (pattern reference for utility main.go structure)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/wc/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: \"wc utility: counting modes, input handling, output formatting, error handling\"\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement all counting modes specified in the wc PRD: line count (-l), word count (-w), byte count (-c), character count (-m), and maximum display line width (-L). When no flags are given, default to showing lines, words, and bytes. Read the PRD for exact flag semantics, definitions, and interactions.\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Handle all input sources specified in the wc PRD: named file arguments on the command line, stdin when no files are given, and the special filename '-' as an alias for stdin. Process multiple files sequentially.\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Format output to match GNU wc: right-aligned count columns with dynamic width, filename printed after counts when processing file arguments, a 'total' line when two or more files are processed. Read the PRD for exact formatting rules.\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Implement exit codes and error handling per the wc PRD: exit 0 when all files processed successfully, exit 1 if any file cannot be opened or read. Print per-file errors to stderr and continue processing remaining files.\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Follow the cmd/ts/main.go pattern for program structure: single main.go file, flag parsing with Go standard library flag package, main() delegates to a run() function.\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Use only the Go standard library for I/O (bufio, os, io, fmt, unicode/utf8). cmd/ packages do not import golang.org/x/sys directly -- that dependency is encapsulated in pkg/sys/.\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"go build ./cmd/wc/ succeeds with no errors.\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"go vet ./cmd/wc/ reports no issues.\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"bin/wc with no flags on a multi-line text file prints three right-aligned numbers (lines, words, bytes) followed by the filename.\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"bin/wc with each individual flag (-l, -w, -c, -m, -L) prints only the corresponding count. bin/wc on multiple files prints per-file lines and a total line.\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":18713,"cache_read_input_tokens":16066,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":18713},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"259f38bf-bda2-4360-9700-53419c75d7a7","uuid":"91247163-171d-4129-8e9f-a8ce92487d66"}
